+### 2b. Rough cut (raw takes only)
+
+Skip this when the creator already cut the take (step 3 finds their cuts). On a
+raw take, propose the cuts before measuring anything:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/autocut.py propose public/recordings/name.mp4 public/recordings/name.words.json
+```
+
+It writes `name.cuts.json` and prints every cut in frames: **silences** (head,
+tail and pauses over 0.35 s, keeping 0.08 s of air each side), **fillers** whisper
+did write (eh, em, mmm), **retakes** (the same 3+ words said again within 20 s:
+the first try goes, cut to the second try's first word) and **unworded voice**
+(sound with no transcribed word, usually a filler whisper dropped; `apply: false`
+by default, check by ear). Show the list, let the creator flip `apply` per row,
+then:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/autocut.py apply public/recordings/name.mp4
+node scripts/transcribe.mjs public/recordings/name.cut.mp4
+```
+
+`name.cut.mp4` is the new master: transcribe it once (whisper times it better
+than the long take, whose pauses it smears words into) and run everything from
+step 3 on it. Tune with `--silence-db -35` (raise to -30 in a noisy room),
+`--min-silence 0.35` (lower for a faster edit) and `--pad 0.08`. Fast talkers
+take `--min-silence 0.25`.
