+## Beat grid
+
+With a bed in, graphic hits that are not tied to a word land on its beats, so
+the edit "sounds" right. Get the grid in composition frames:
+
+```bash
+python scripts/beat-grid.py "public/music pack/track.mp3" --start START_S --frames DUR
+```
+
+It prints the BPM and each beat frame (`|` marks an assumed downbeat: confirm by
+ear before landing a drop on it). Rules:
+
+- **Voice wins.** A graphic tied to a spoken word stays on the word. Snap only
+  hits that are free: transitions, section cards, list items between phrases,
+  stretches with no speech.
+- Snap when a hit sits within 2 frames of a beat; big moments go on beats,
+  secondary ones on the half beat.
+- Choosing `START_S` so a downbeat lands on a cut: `START_S = beatTime - cutFrame / 30`.
+
